# Source: openwrt/openwrt PR #24872 "airoha: grow the small RX rings"（Vitaliy Sochnev，2026-09-10，
#   backport 自 kernel 7.4 队列提交 e84b89f17a12，Acked-by Lorenzo Bianconi）
#   https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/24872
# Upstream: open（#24872，mergeable_state=blocked）；合入后删除本层补丁，改 FIXES 状态
# Reason: ring 4 = 共享 "force to CPU" 环，airoha_fe_vip_setup() 把 BOOTP、PPPoE Discovery、
#   PPP LCP/IPCP/CHAP/PAP/IPv6CP、ISAKMP、DHCPv6、SIP、LLDP 全导到它（两个 CDM 的
#   CDM_VIP_QSEL_MASK 都 =4）。16 描述符只占 4096B page 的 512B，硬件跑到环尾不在边界停下，
#   page 尾部是 32B 周期的"描述符形状"数据 → 硬件跑过已投递描述符、在非环内 slot 找不到
#   buffer，标 DROP 但仍写描述符结构 → 越过 page 就写进内核内存。后果：DHCP/PPPoE 握手期
#   内核 panic（实测垃圾指针落在 cpufreq dbs_irq_work / scheduler / nf_conntrack 上，5 次），
#   或 PPPoE 协商永不完成（REG_RX_DMA_IDX 前进而 REG_RX_CPU_IDX 卡在 15）。
#   修法：RX_DSCP_NUM() fallback 16 → 32（vendor SDK 默认，实测 16↔32 之间是硬件边界），
#   ring 4 → 128（与 ring 2/11/15 一致）。代价 1088 个额外描述符（约 2.1MiB RX buffer +
#   34KiB coherent desc）。作者明确否定了 SoC 限定：ring 4 与 VIP 分类是全驱动共享，无 DT/
#   硬件属性区分 → **对 AN7581 同样适用**。
# 与本地关系：本仓 9001（板级 dts）/9025（no-carrier rx stats）/9038（PCS 校准）/9041（SerDes）
#   均不触碰 airoha_eth.h 的 RX_DSCP_NUM 宏 → 零冲突（已核对文件与 hunk 区）；
#   本补丁的 916-02 机械头同步会改变 vendor/fanboy/11（LRO）的 916-02 基线，MANIFEST 中
#   9042 置于 vendor/11 **之前**应用（本补丁同时把 916-02 内层上下文 16→32 同步好，
#   vendor/11 的 @@ -553,8 段在 9042 之后仍可应用——见应用顺序验证记录）。
# 验证：对 openwrt main 3de9bf7 树真实应用通过（git apply）；本补丁新增的内层
#   182-v7.4-net-airoha-grow-the-small-RX-rings.patch 逐字节等同上游 PR。
From: Vitaliy Sochnev <sochnev.v.74@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] airoha: grow the small RX rings

Raise the RX_DSCP_NUM() fallback from 16 to 32, the vendor SDK default,
and give ring 4 the 128 descriptors already used for rings 2/11/15.

Ring 4 is the shared "force to CPU" ring that airoha_fe_vip_setup()
routes BOOTP, PPPoE Discovery, PPP LCP/IPCP/CHAP/PAP/IPv6CP, ISAKMP,
DHCPv6, SIP and LLDP onto, so it sees the same bursty non-hashed traffic
as the rings already on 128 while sitting on the smallest allowance.
Both CDMs forward to it: REG_CDM_FWD_CFG(1) and (2) each set
CDM_VIP_QSEL_MASK to 4.

Ring 4 and the VIP classification feeding it are shared driver-wide, with
no DT or hardware property distinguishing one variant's ring 4 from
another's, so this is not scoped to a particular SoC.

Signed-off-by: Vitaliy Sochnev <sochnev.v.74@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/target/linux/airoha/patches-6.18/182-v7.4-net-airoha-grow-the-small-RX-rings.patch b/target/linux/airoha/patches-6.18/182-v7.4-net-airoha-grow-the-small-RX-rings.patch
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000000..3a21a65022acab
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/airoha/patches-6.18/182-v7.4-net-airoha-grow-the-small-RX-rings.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+From e84b89f17a12a7cfc526eb1c18ac02e8777e18c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Vitaliy Sochnev <sochnev.v.74@gmail.com>
+Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 19:32:54 +0100
+Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: grow the small RX rings
+
+Raise the RX_DSCP_NUM() fallback from 16 to 32, the vendor SDK default,
+and give ring 4 the 128 descriptors already used for rings 2/11/15.
+
+Ring 4 is the shared "force to CPU" ring that airoha_fe_vip_setup()
+routes BOOTP, PPPoE Discovery, PPP LCP/IPCP/CHAP/PAP/IPv6CP, ISAKMP,
+DHCPv6, SIP and LLDP onto, so it sees the same bursty non-hashed traffic
+as the rings already on 128 while sitting on the smallest allowance.
+Both CDMs forward to it: REG_CDM_FWD_CFG(1) and (2) each set
+CDM_VIP_QSEL_MASK to 4.
+
+The NO_CPU_DSCP fix does not cover this. With it in place, at 16
+descriptors the ring still dies during PPPoE negotiation on a Nokia
+XG-040G-MF: over 6455 devmem samples in 60 s, REG_RX_DMA_IDX advanced
+0x2c -> 0x52 while REG_RX_CPU_IDX stayed at 15, descriptor 15 had DONE
+set on a 60-byte frame, descriptors 0-14 were empty, and q->tail was 0.
+Hw had completed a descriptor the strictly sequential consumer in
+airoha_qdma_rx_process() cannot reach, and negotiation never completes.
+At 16 DHCP still works while PPPoE does not: a dial-up bursts Discovery,
+LCP, IPCP and CHAP where DHCP sends one packet every ~150 s. With this
+series, 508 forced reconnects over 20 h saw no recurrence.
+
+RX_DONE_INT_MASK covers all 32 rings on both QDMA instances, so this
+costs 544 more descriptors per instance, 1088 in total: 2.1 MiB of RX
+buffers at PAGE_SIZE/2 each, plus 34 KiB of coherent descriptor memory.
+
+Ring 4 and the VIP classification feeding it are shared driver-wide, with
+no DT or hardware property distinguishing one variant's ring 4 from
+another's, so this is not scoped to a particular SoC.
+
+Acked-by: Lorenzo Bianconi <lorenzo@kernel.org>
+Signed-off-by: Vitaliy Sochnev <sochnev.v.74@gmail.com>
+Link: https://patch.msgid.link/978fe95e4c5ddb05ceb7d8c4d00ea2d2203b79d0.1788286284.git.sochnev.v.74@gmail.com
+Signed-off-by: Jakub Kicinski <kuba@kernel.org>
+---
+ drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h | 3 ++-
+ 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
+
+--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
++++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
+@@ -40,9 +40,10 @@
+ #define TX_DSCP_NUM			1024
+ #define RX_DSCP_NUM(_n)			\
+ 	((_n) ==  2 ? 128 :		\
++	 (_n) ==  4 ? 128 :		\
+ 	 (_n) == 11 ? 128 :		\
+ 	 (_n) == 15 ? 128 :		\
+-	 (_n) ==  0 ? 1024 : 16)
++	 (_n) ==  0 ? 1024 : 32)
+ 
+ #define PSE_RSV_PAGES			128
+ #define PSE_QUEUE_RSV_PAGES		64
